    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Stylish A-Rated Family Home in an Exceptional Town Location\nCME Naas welcome you to 8 Whitethorn Place an exceptional A rated, nearly new home, beautifully presented and ready to walk into! Ideally positioned within the highly regarded Whitethorn Village Development, just moments from the vibrant centre of Naas Town, No.8 has been elegantly decorated throughout by the house proud owner and also benefits from a low maintenance, sunny, southerly facing rear garden. This impressive home, built by Cairn, combines contemporary style, energy efficiency, and superb family living in one of Naas' most convenient residential settings and it's position within the development offers a peaceful cul de sac location, adjacent to the popular walking route of Rathasker Lane. The property provides a cobblelock driveway allowing off-street parking for 2 cars, while gated side access leads to an enviable southerly facing rear garden, which is paved and low maintenance with a steel shed which provides excellent storage. Inside, you will find most spacious and well laid out accommodation which is bathed in natural light and presented impeccably. Commuters will particularly appreciate the superb connectivity, with easy access to the M7 motorway and the nearby Sallins Arrow rail service providing a convenient route to Dublin City Centre. The bustling Town of Naas offers an extensive range of amenities including supermarkets, shops and boutiques, Artisan bakeries and coffee shops, quality restaurants as well as an excellent range of creches, primary and secondary schools, gyms and playgrounds. Don't miss out on this excellent opportunity; contact our Naas office to arrange a viewing!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall: c.1.1m x 4.7m\nAttractive laminate word flooring. Large storage area under stairs. Large side window affording natural light. Spotlights to ceiling.\n\nGuest WC: c. 1.5m x 1.6m \nWith WC, wash hand basin, tiled floor and heated towel radiator. \n\nSittingroom: c. 4.7 x 3.9m\nSpacious proportions with large picture window. Laminate wood floor.\n\nKitchen/Dining: \nc. 4.7m x 5.2m\nContemporary style kitchen with anthracite tone cabinetry comprising of wall and floor units incorporating double oven, microwave, fridge freezer, dishwasher and ceramic hob. Large window and French doors allowing access to the southerly facing garden. Laminate wood flooring.\n\nUtility Room: c. 3.1m x 2.4m\nPlumbed for washing machine, excellent storage. Laminate wood flooring.\n\nLanding: \nQuality carpeted floor. Hotpress. Access to attic via Stira stairs.\n\nMaster Bedroom: c.4.3m x 5.2\nExtremely bright and spacious proportions. 2 Large windows affording maximum light. Quality laminate flooring. Floor to ceiling fitted wardrobes.\n\nEnsuite: c. 1.7m x 2.2m\nWith spacious shower enclosure, WC, wash hand basin. Tiled walls and floors. \n\nBedroom 2: c.5m x 2.2m\nRear Aspect. Floor to ceiling wardrobes. Laminate flooring. \n\nBedroom 3: c.5m x 2.2m\nRear aspect. Quality laminate flooring. \n\nBathroom: c. 1.8m x 3.1m\nWith bath, separate shower enclosure, WC and wash hand basin. Tiled walls & floor. Heated towel rail.\n\nOutside: \nTo the front there is a double cobblelock driveway with space for two cars. Gated side entrance to sunny, south west facing garden."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious 3 bedroom home extending to c.110sqm\nEnergy efficient “A” rated property\nAir to water Heat Pump \nBright and well proportioned throughout with an abundance of natural light \nSoutherly facing, low maintenance rear garden \nMaster Bedroom En-suite\nGuest WC & Utility Room with excellent storage\nStira stairs to attic\nOutside tap, light and power point\nCul de sac location\nWalking distance to Town Centre and Osprey Hotel and Leisure Centre"
      },
